image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1941\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1941,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1309990,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;The Wholehearted Woman Retreat with Erin Lee in Siem Reap Cambodia&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The Wholehearted Woman Retreat with Erin Lee in Siem Reap Cambodia&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://erinmindfulmoments.substack.com/i/195494180?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"The Wholehearted Woman Retreat with Erin Lee in Siem Reap Cambodia\" title=\"The Wholehearted Woman Retreat with Erin Lee in Siem Reap Cambodia\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IQsg!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ffd62b7f4-2d71-46b7-8460-c3a17574a16d_2296x3061.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://vigeoretreats.com/retreat/the-wholehearted-woman-retreat/&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Join Erin at Angkor Wat&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://vigeoretreats.com/retreat/the-wholehearted-woman-retreat/\"><span>Join Erin at Angkor Wat</span></a></p>",
  "body_text": "What does it mean to truly be honest? Not just with others, but with ourselves?\n\nIn Buddhist teachings, there’s a quality of heart called sacca — often translated as truthfulness or authenticity. \n\nAnd it’s more than just not lying. \n\nIt’s about living in alignment with reality: making sure our words, actions, and intentions actually match up.\n\nIn everyday life, this may be harder than it sounds.\n\nWe live in an age of curated identities. Social media nudges us into performance mode — presenting the best version of ourselves rather than the real one. \n\nSacca invites us to pause and ask: Am I who I appear to be?\n\nIt also shows up in subtler ways. \n\nWhen we do something kind, is there a small ego boost in it? When we set a boundary, is fear quietly driving that decision? When we love someone, is it truly unconditional — or does it come with strings?\n\nNone of this is about self-judgment. It’s simply about seeing clearly.\n\nAnd there’s a practical piece too: keeping our word. \n\nWhen we make a commitment, do you follow through?\n\nCultivating this kind of honesty — gently, without self-criticism — is one of the most grounding things we can do for ourselves and for everyone around us.\n\n---\n\nAt Take A Pause Live over 20 & 21 June 2026, we practiced body awareness and learned to meet each moment of our experience truthfully, as it it. We closed the session with a reading of the poem Telescope by Louise Glück. \n\nMeditation Practice\n\nTap Play to Practice Together:\n\nThis post is free for 4 weeks, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. Upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nThe Wholehearted Woman Retreat\n\nA five-day mindfulness retreat into quiet wisdom and the light within\n\n1-5 October 2026\nSiem Reap, Cambodia\n\nLed by Erin Lee\n\nJoin Erin at Angkor Wat",
